-- title:
--   Proposition 4.2 — norm equivalence under the gap ensuring condition (corrected: under $\max_k d(y^{t,0},y^{t,k})\le r$)
-- statement:
--   **Proposition 4.2 (corrected).** Consider a run of Algorithm 1 (with arbitrary positive stepsizes) along which the selection is $(\gamma,r)$-gap ensuring (Assumption 4.2). Then at every iteration $t\ge1$ with
--
--   $$
--   \max_{k\in[m]} d(y^{t,0},y^{t,k})\le r ,
--   $$
--
--   every $v\in T_{y^{t,0}}M$ satisfies
--
--   $$
--   (1-\sqrt m\,\gamma)\,\|v\|_{y^{t,0}}\le\|v\|_{y^{t,0},\mathcal P}\le(1+\sqrt m\,\gamma)\,\|v\|_{y^{t,0}} .
--   $$
--
--   The seminorm $\|\cdot\|_{y^{t,0},\mathcal P}$ built from the transported projections $P_{t,k}$ is thus equivalent to the Riemannian norm at $y^{t,0}$ whenever the inner loop stays within distance $r$. This lets the decrease bound (11), stated in $\|\cdot\|_{y^{t,0},\mathcal P}$, be turned into a bound in $\|\nabla f(y^{t,0})\|_{y^{t,0}}$.
--
--   **Formalization Note** Lean's `k : Fin m` is the paper's step $k+1$, so the proviso ranges over $y^{t,1},\dots,y^{t,m}$.
--
--   Differences from the source:
--   - correction: the norm equivalence at any iteration t ≥ 1 → the norm equivalence at iterations t ≥ 1 with max_{k∈[m]} d(y^{t,0}, y^{t,k}) ≤ r; reason: the printed statement is false. Counterexample: ℝ² with Exp_x(v) = x + v, f = ½‖x‖², m = 2, γ = 1/10, r = 1, L_k = 1, stepsizes 1, x⁰ = (2, 0), rule P(·,1) = Π_{e₁} and P(·,2) = Π_{e₂} if d(y^{t,0}, y^{t,1}) ≤ r, Π_{e₁} otherwise; the rule is (1/10, 1)-gap ensuring, but at t = 1, y^{1,1} = 0 is at distance 2 > r and ‖e₂‖_{y,P} = 0 < 1 − √2/10. Remark 4.1 (p.11) states the result with this proviso, and Lemma 4.4 uses it only then
--   - generalization: a connected, geodesically complete Riemannian manifold with its Riemannian distance, exponential map, parallel transport and Riemannian gradient → an abstract metric space with finite-dimensional inner-product fibres, an exp map and isometric transports satisfying (A1) and (A2), and any function f with any gradient field; reason: Mathlib has no exponential map or parallel transport, and the paper's objects satisfy (A1), (A2) and isometry by the §2 facts (p.4)
--   - generalization: P (γ, r)-gap ensuring for every sequence generated by Algorithm 1 → Assumption 4.2 along one given run whose subspaces are data; reason: every run of every gap ensuring rule is such a run
--   - generalization: transport Γ^{y^{t,0}}_{y^{t,k−1}} along an unspecified geodesic → transport along the geodesic fixed by an arbitrary connecting vector w_{t,k}; reason: the statement holds for every choice
--   - encoding: inner index k ∈ [m] = {1,…,m} → k : Fin m = {0,…,m−1}; reason: index shift only
-- source:
--   Gutman & Ho-Nguyen, Coordinate Descent Without Coordinates, arXiv:1912.10627v3, Proposition 4.2, p.11 (proviso from Remark 4.1, p.11)

import Mathlib
import Definitions.Def_TSDRiem_RiemSetting
import Definitions.Def_TSDRiem_TSDRun
import Definitions.Def_TSDRiem_TSDRun_seminormP
import Definitions.Def_TSDRiem_TSDRun_GapEnsuring

namespace TSDRiem

/-- **Proposition 4.2 (corrected).** If the rule is `(γ, r)`-gap ensuring, then at any iteration
`t ≥ 1` of Algorithm 1 with `max_{k∈[m]} d(y^{t,0}, y^{t,k}) ≤ r`,
`(1 − √m γ)‖·‖_{y^{t,0}} ≤ ‖·‖_{y^{t,0},P} ≤ (1 + √m γ)‖·‖_{y^{t,0}}`.

Gutman & Ho-Nguyen, Coordinate Descent Without Coordinates, arXiv:1912.10627v3,
Proposition 4.2, p.11.

Formalization Note (correction): the printed proposition omits the proviso
`max_{k∈[m]} d(y^{t,0}, y^{t,k}) ≤ r`, under which alone Assumption 4.2 supplies the orthogonal
decomposition; Remark 4.1 (p.11) states the result with it, and Lemma 4.4 uses it only then.
Without it the printed statement is false (ℝ², `m = 2`, `γ = 1/10`, `r = 1`, `f = ½‖x‖²`,
`x⁰ = (2, 0)`, rule `P(·,1) = Π_{e₁}`, `P(·,2) = Π_{e₂}` if `d(y^{t,0}, y^{t,1}) ≤ r` and `Π_{e₁}`
otherwise: at `t = 1`, `‖e₂‖_{y,P} = 0 < 1 − √2/10`). The stepsizes are arbitrary positive
numbers, as in Algorithm 1. Lean's `k : Fin m` is the paper's `k + 1`. -/
theorem proposition_4_2 {M : Type*} [MetricSpace M] {T : M → Type*}
    [∀ x, NormedAddCommGroup (T x)] [∀ x, InnerProductSpace ℝ (T x)]
    [∀ x, FiniteDimensional ℝ (T x)] (S : RiemSetting M T) (grad : (x : M) → T x) {m : ℕ}
    (R : TSDRun S grad m) (γ r : ℝ) (h42 : R.GapEnsuring γ r) (t : ℕ) (ht : 1 ≤ t)
    (hnear : ∀ k : Fin m, dist (R.y t 0) (R.y t k.succ) ≤ r) (v : T (R.y t 0)) :
    (1 - Real.sqrt m * γ) * ‖v‖ ≤ R.seminormP t v ∧
      R.seminormP t v ≤ (1 + Real.sqrt m * γ) * ‖v‖ := by sorry

end TSDRiem
